## What this is

The **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** game repository — a single shipped {{GENRE_TITLE}}
title in the Ship Shit Games portfolio. Scaffolded with `shipshitgames new`.

This repo owns:

- The shipped game (gameplay, scenes, UI overlays, content/data tables).
- Game-specific runtime assets, audio, and art that this title ships.

This repo does **not** own:

- The reusable engine. It consumes `{{ENGINE_PACKAGE}}` as a published package
  (or a temporary local `bun link` bridge for unpublished engine work). See
  `repo-boundary.md`.
- Studio tooling (asset generation, the studio site/app/desktop). That lives in
  `shipshitgames/shipshit.games`.

## Engine

`{{ENGINE_PACKAGE}}` is the canonical org-level engine: the Game/Context/Systems
spine, swappable camera rig, embodied movement + collision + world bounds, the
agent/steering + spawn + wave-director seams, the HUD snapshot shell, input
bindings, and replicated presence. This game wires its {{GENRE_TITLE}} content
into those seams; it never edits the engine in place.

## Lore

Deadrot canon is vendored as a git submodule at `{{LORE_PATH}}`
(`git submodule update --init {{LORE_PATH}}`). Treat it as read-only canon;
do not author canon here.

## Conventions

- Bun + Turborepo conventions, mirroring the studio monorepo.
- Keep gameplay imperative and Three.js-centered; React for overlays only.
- Use the `worktree` skill to start issues; `session-start`/`session-end` to
  bookend work.
